 "text": "In 1950, the U.S. Navy sprayed bacteria over San Francisco. On purpose. It was called Operation Sea Spray. The test? How would a germ attack spread? The Army later estimated almost everyone in the city breathed it in. Soon after, a rare infection showed up at a local hospital. One patient, Edward Nevin, died. The Army denied any link. Here's the trick. Nobody complains about a test they don't know exists. It stayed secret until 1976. Follow for more dark psychology.",
